CONFIRMED: at every control site/resolution with both a low- and high-QC tier available, low P_F_QC rows are far more often bit-identical to P_ERA than high P_F_QC rows -- i.e. P_F_QC near 0 = fully ERA-filled, P_F_QC near 1 = genuinely measured (higher = more measured). This matches CLAUDE.md's System-1 fraction convention and this repo's prior network-wide findings (era5_precip_units_v3_partA.R / v4.R; review/diagnostics/precip_site_filter/report.md). Used throughout this project: measured share = P_F_QC; ERA-filled share = 1 - P_F_QC.
